.TH GERRY 1 "August 2026" "gerrymander" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gerry \- hostname and port control plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gerry
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gerry
is one authority for who owns which hostname in a wildcard zone, and which
process owns which port on a dev machine. The same binary, model, and CLI
run on a laptop (TLS proxy, embedded DNS, process supervision) and in
production (registry, Kubernetes observer and route actuator).
.SH FIRST RUN
.TP
.B gerry bootstrap [\-\-no\-setup]
The whole first run as one idempotent command: daemon on login, DNS for
dev zones, TLS trust. Skips the service when a daemon already serves the
API.
.TP
.B gerry init [\-\-name P] [\-\-zone Z] [\-\-yes]
Scaffold gerrymander.yaml in the current project. Detects the dev command
from package.json and the lockfile; for vite projects, offers to install
gerrymander\-vite and wire vite.config itself.
.SH DAILY COMMANDS
.TP
.B gerry dev [service] [\-f file]
Apply the manifest, grant sticky ports, and run the declared dev:
commands, prefixed, with group shutdown.
.TP
.B gerry run \-\-owner O \-\- CMD [args...]
Claim O's sticky port, then exec CMD with PORT exported and any literal
{PORT} in the arguments replaced.
.TP
.B gerry status
The doctor: daemon, DNS, proxy, trust, tailnet checks, each failure with
its exact fix.
.TP
.B gerry tailnet
Guided setup for dev hostnames across a tailscale network: probes
machine\-subdomain resolution, split DNS and machine\-name ports, and
walks through whatever is missing. Re\-running verifies each change.
.SH REGISTRY
.TP
.B gerry claim \-\-zone Z \-\-label L [\-\-owner O] [\-\-kind tenant|platform] [\-\-hold]
Claim a hostname. Conflicts return the reason and suggestions.
.TP
.B gerry avail \-\-zone Z \-\-label L
Availability check with why\-not and suggestions.
.TP
.B gerry ls [\-\-zone Z] [\-\-owner O]
List allocations.
.TP
.B gerry rename <fqdn> <label>
Atomic rename; id, owner, routes and history survive.
.TP
.B gerry release \-\-id N
Release an allocation.
.TP
.B gerry port \-\-owner O [\-\-pool dev]
Sticky port: the same owner always receives the same port.
.TP
.B gerry zone add|rm, gerry token create|ls|revoke, gerry conflicts
Zones, scoped API credentials, and observer findings.
.SH MACHINE LIFECYCLE
.TP
.B gerry service install|status|restart|uninstall
Run the daemon on login (launchd on macOS, systemd \-\-user on Linux).
.TP
.B gerry trust [\-\-print]
Install the daemon's CA into the system trust store. Phones fetch
/v1/ca.crt from the daemon instead.
.TP
.B gerry setup [\-\-print] / gerry uninstall [\-\-yes] [\-\-purge]
Wire (and fully unwire) DNS and trust. Everything written is
marker\-tagged; uninstall removes only gerry's own marks and can never
break DNS it did not create.
.TP
.B gerry update [\-\-check]
Self\-update from the latest release. Homebrew installs defer to brew.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GERRY_API
Daemon address (default http://127.0.0.1:4780).
.TP
.B GERRY_API_KEY
Bearer credential; scoped tokens from `gerry token` work here too.
.TP
.B GERRY_TLD
Default TLD for `gerry init` scaffolds (default: test).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gerrymander/
Database, CA material, config, and logs (host mode).
.TP
.I gerrymander.yaml
Per\-project manifest: zone, services, hostnames, dev commands.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: https://nano112.github.io/gerrymander
